<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>APPROVED yellow3 Insights Subscribe v1.0</title>
<!-- Approved design handover v1.0, 23 August 2026. Approved by Thomas
     Christian Melskens. Design owner ChatGPT. This file is the intake
     record for research/port_approved_css.py: the stylesheet block below is the
     package stylesheet from reference-prototype/app/globals.css and the
     body is the approved markup from reference-prototype/app/page.tsx.
     The `@import "tailwindcss"` line is dropped: it is a build directive,
     not design CSS, and the package markup uses no Tailwind utility.
     Nothing else is altered. -->
<style>

:root {
  --yellow: #ffe500;
  --ink: #171717;
  --black: #0e0e0e;
  --muted: #6b6b6b;
  --line: #d5d7d7;
  --soft: #f1f3f3;
  --paper: #ffffff;
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }

body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--paper);
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

a { color: inherit; }
button, input { font: inherit; }

.shell { width: min(1360px, calc(100% - 80px)); margin: 0 auto; }

.button span,
.text-link span,
.preview-link span { margin-left: 10px; }

.subscribe-hero { padding: 38px 0 76px; }

.breadcrumb {
  display: flex;
  gap: 11px;
  margin: 0 0 32px;
  color: #8a8a8a;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: .15em;
}

.breadcrumb a { text-decoration: none; }
.signal-line { height: 7px; background: var(--yellow); }

.hero-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.7fr) minmax(300px, .7fr);
  gap: 86px;
  padding-top: 62px;
}

.kicker,
.control-label,
.issue-label,
.entry-meta {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: .16em;
}

.kicker { color: #777; }
.kicker-light { color: #a8a8a8; }

.hero-grid h1 {
  max-width: 850px;
  margin: 18px 0 24px;
  font-size: clamp(58px, 6.2vw, 90px);
  font-weight: 400;
  letter-spacing: -.055em;
  line-height: .97;
}

.hero-copy {
  max-width: 670px;
  margin: 0;
  color: #5d5d5d;
  font-size: 20px;
  line-height: 1.55;
}

.hero-aside {
  align-self: end;
  padding: 30px 0 10px 36px;
  border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
}

.aside-label { margin: 0 0 18px; color: #777; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .16em; }
.aside-lede { margin: 0 0 24px; font-size: 22px; }
.hero-aside ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; color: #666; }
.hero-aside li { padding: 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; }

.feed-action-section { background: var(--black); color: #fff; }

.feed-action-grid {
  min-height: 455px;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: .82fr 1.18fr;
}

.feed-intro { padding: 76px 70px 70px 0; border-right: 1px solid #383838; }
.feed-intro h2 { margin: 22px 0 0; font-size: clamp(40px, 4vw, 62px); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.045em; line-height: 1.02; }

.feed-control { padding: 76px 0 54px 76px; }
.control-label { color: #999; }
.feed-url { margin: 18px 0 20px; padding-bottom: 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid #464646; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.3vw, 34px); letter-spacing: -.025em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.control-copy { max-width: 670px; margin: 0; color: #b7b7b7; }
.control-actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 32px; }

.button {
  min-height: 49px;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: 0;
  padding: 13px 20px;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: .08em;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.button-yellow { background: var(--yellow); color: var(--ink); }
.button-light { border-color: #666; background: transparent; color: #fff; }
.button:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--yellow); outline-offset: 4px; }

.preview-link {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-top: 34px;
  color: #aaa;
  font-size: 10px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: .12em;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.how-section { padding: 96px 0 110px; }
.section-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .35fr 1fr; gap: 50px; align-items: start; }
.section-heading h2 { max-width: 760px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(38px, 4.3vw, 64px); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.045em; line-height: 1.05; }

.steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 72px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
.steps article { min-height: 255px; padding: 30px 38px 24px 0; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
.steps article + article { padding-left: 38px; }
.steps article:last-child { border-right: 0; }
.step-number { margin: 0 0 42px; color: #8a8a8a; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .14em; }
.steps h3 { margin: 0 0 15px; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
.steps article > p:last-child { margin: 0; color: #666; }

.latest-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--soft); }
.latest-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .72fr 1.28fr; gap: 86px; padding-top: 94px; padding-bottom: 100px; }
.latest-heading { padding-right: 50px; }
.latest-heading h2 { margin: 18px 0 24px; font-size: clamp(40px, 4vw, 60px); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.045em; line-height: 1.05; }
.latest-heading > p:last-child { color: #666; }
.latest-list { border-top: 1px solid #bfc2c2; }
.latest-list article { padding: 30px 0 32px; border-bottom: 1px solid #c9cccc; }
.issue-label { color: #777; }
.latest-list h3 { margin: 10px 0 10px; font-size: 27px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.025em; line-height: 1.15; }
.latest-list article > p:last-child { max-width: 760px; margin: 0; color: #666; }
.text-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 30px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em; text-decoration: none; }

.feed-view { min-height: 100vh; background: #fff; }
.feed-view-intro { width: min(1240px, calc(100% - 72px)); display: grid; grid-template-columns: .9fr .8fr; gap: 100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 52px 0 62px; position: relative; }
.feed-view-intro .signal-line { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; }
.feed-view-intro h1 { margin: 16px 0 0; font-size: clamp(50px, 5.5vw, 76px); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.05em; line-height: 1; }
.feed-view-intro > p { align-self: end; margin: 0; padding-left: 34px; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); color: #666; font-size: 17px; }
.feed-address-band { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr auto; gap: 32px; align-items: center; padding: 24px max(36px, calc((100vw - 1240px) / 2)); background: var(--black); color: #fff; }
.feed-address-band span { color: #999; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; }
.feed-address-band strong { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 400; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.feed-address-band a { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em; text-decoration: none; }
.feed-entries { width: min(1240px, calc(100% - 72px)); margin: 0 auto; }
.feed-entries article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 70px 1fr 40px; gap: 28px; padding: 40px 0 42px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
.entry-index { margin: 6px 0 0; color: #999; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .14em; }
.entry-meta { color: #777; }
.feed-entries h2 { margin: 12px 0 12px; font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 42px); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.035em; line-height: 1.08; }
.feed-entries article div > p:last-child { max-width: 820px; margin: 0; color: #666; }
.entry-arrow { align-self: center; font-size: 27px; }
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .shell { width: min(100% - 36px, 760px); }
  .hero-grid, .feed-action-grid, .latest-grid, .section-heading { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .hero-grid { gap: 46px; }
  .hero-aside { align-self: auto; }
  .feed-intro { padding-right: 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #383838; }
  .feed-control { padding-left: 0; }
  .steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .steps article, .steps article + article { min-height: 0; padding: 28px 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .step-number { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .feed-view-intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 38px; }
  .feed-view-intro > p { align-self: auto; }
  .feed-address-band { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}

@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .subscribe-hero { padding-top: 26px; }
  .hero-grid { padding-top: 42px; }
  .hero-grid h1 { font-size: 54px; }
  .hero-copy { font-size: 17px; }
  .hero-aside { padding-left: 20px; }
  .feed-action-grid { min-height: 0; }
  .feed-intro, .feed-control { padding-top: 52px; padding-bottom: 48px; }
  .control-actions { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
  .button { width: 100%; }
  .how-section { padding: 72px 0; }
  .latest-grid { gap: 44px; padding-top: 72px; }
  .feed-view-intro, .feed-entries { width: calc(100% - 36px); }
  .feed-view-intro { padding-top: 44px; }
  .feed-view-intro > p { padding-left: 20px; }
  .feed-address-band { padding: 24px 18px; }
  .feed-entries article { grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .entry-arrow { display: none; }
}
</style></head>
<body>
<!-- Approved markup, reference-prototype/app/page.tsx, JSX resolved to HTML.
     The three .latest-list articles are the package's LAYOUT PLACEHOLDERS and
     are marked as such: 05-CONTENT-CONTRACT.md and Lock 07 forbid them
     shipping. Production fills that list from the publication records that
     generate /feed.xml - see research/gen_subscribe.py. -->
<main>
  <section class="subscribe-hero shell">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="https://www.yellow3.io/insights/">INSIGHTS</a><span>/</span>SUBSCRIBE</p>
    <div class="signal-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">YELLOW3 INSIGHTS</p>
        <h1>Follow the work,<br>not the noise.</h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">New yellow3 research, analysis and evidence records, delivered directly through RSS whenever we publish.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-aside" aria-label="Feed principles">
        <p class="aside-label">THE FEED</p>
        <p class="aside-lede">Chronological by design.</p>
        <ul><li>No account.</li><li>No inbox.</li><li>No algorithm deciding what you see.</li></ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="feed-action-section">
    <div class="shell feed-action-grid">
      <div class="feed-intro">
        <p class="kicker kicker-light">OFFICIAL RSS FEED</p>
        <h2>One address.<br>Every new publication.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feed-control">
        <p class="control-label">FEED ADDRESS</p>
        <p class="feed-url">https://www.yellow3.io/feed.xml</p>
        <p class="control-copy">Copy this address into any RSS reader, or open the feed to inspect the latest published entries.</p>
        <div class="control-actions">
          <button class="button button-yellow" type="button">COPY FEED ADDRESS</button>
          <a class="button button-light" href="https://www.yellow3.io/feed.xml">OPEN RSS FEED <span>&#8594;</span></a>
        </div>
        <a class="preview-link" href="/feed-preview">VIEW THE APPROVED BROWSER PRESENTATION <span>&#8594;</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="how-section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="kicker">HOW IT WORKS</p>
      <h2>Direct publishing, without another platform.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <article><p class="step-number">01</p><h3>Copy the feed address.</h3><p>The same permanent address carries every future yellow3 Insights publication.</p></article>
      <article><p class="step-number">02</p><h3>Add it to your reader.</h3><p>Paste the address into the RSS reader you already use. No yellow3 account is required.</p></article>
      <article><p class="step-number">03</p><h3>Receive new work in order.</h3><p>New entries appear chronologically when yellow3 publishes them. Nothing is ranked or promoted.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="latest-section">
    <div class="shell latest-grid">
      <div class="latest-heading">
        <p class="kicker">IN THE FEED</p>
        <h2>The latest yellow3 Insights.</h2>
        <p>Research, frameworks and sourced analysis across emerging technology, regulation and the systems businesses must operate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="latest-list">
        <article><p class="issue-label">PLACEHOLDER</p><h3>Layout placeholder, not approved content</h3><p>Replaced at build time from the publication records.</p></article>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://www.yellow3.io/insights/">VIEW ALL INSIGHTS <span>&#8594;</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</body></html>
